// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row try_operator_result_local_borrow_escape_admitted (tier 1, `admits`).
// ILLEGAL PROGRAM ADMITTED: a borrow of a LOCAL is carried out of a function through the
// `?` operator, and the reference obtained from it outlives the scope it borrowed.
//
//   fn get<'a>(x: &'a i64) -> Option<&'a i64> { return Option::Some(x); }
//   fn escape() -> Option<&'static i64> { let n: i64 = 9i64; let r: &i64 = get(&n)?; ... }
//
// logosc compiles this CLEAN (cc=0, no diagnostic) and the binary RUNS. `n` is dead at
// the return, so the reference handed back points into the dead frame.
//
// rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 MEASURED 2026-09-17: REFUSES,
//   error[E0515]: cannot return value referencing local variable `n`
// Twin: src/compiler/probes/2026-09-17d-arrlit/rust/nb_try.rs
//
// ⚠ IT IS THE CARRIER, NOT THE BORROW. The SAME escape through a bare `&n`, a tuple
// literal, an array literal, an array repeat and a nested array literal is REFUSED on the
// binary this row is opened against — the array spellings by the `ArrLit` arm landed in
// the same commit as this row. `Try` is a DIFFERENT node kind and `prov_of_raw` has no
// arm for it, so nothing catches this one.
//
// FOUND 2026-09-17d-arrlit, enumerating prov_of_raw's missing arms with tools/dlog
// (`prov_arms.dl`): `Try` is named there with SIX sibling walkers that do have the arm.
// MEASURED UNMOVED by this round's ArrLit arm (armed binary, cc=0) — rowed, not closed,
// because it is a different fact and its own legal direction is unpriced.
// FIX = the program is REFUSED, with a diagnostic naming the escaping borrow.
package try_operator_result_local_borrow_escape_admitted;
fn get<'a>(x: &'a i64) -> Option<&'a i64> {
    return Option::Some(x);
}
fn escape() -> Option<&'static i64> {
    let n: i64 = 9i64;
    let r: &i64 = get(&n)?;
    return Option::Some(r);
}
fn main() -> i32 {
    let o: Option<&i64> = escape();
    return 0i32;
}
